            <div xml:id="d516">

                <pb facs="0906" n="810" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg810"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/4198: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sheffield</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-12-08T11:00:00-07:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 8,
                                1926—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 4:39
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>503. Press today published a telegram dated December 2 from Espinosa, the Foreign
                    Minister of the Sacasa regime at Puerto Cabezas, to the Mexican Foreign Minister
                    requesting Mexican recognition, and a telegram dated December 7 from the Mexican
                    Foreign Minister to Espinosa extending recognition.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sheffield</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
